        <body>
            <div xml:id="d421">

                <pb facs="0756" n="660" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg660"/>

                <head>No. 419.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bingham to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation, Japan</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Yokohama</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-01-14"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 14, 1874</date>.
                        (Received February 21.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 43.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Herewith I beg leave to call your attention
                    to a letter of J. H. Hawes, United States consul at Hakodadi, No. 288, dated the
                    6th instant, inclosure No. 1; and to my reply thereto, inclosure No. 2.</p>
                <p>You will observe that the case presented by Mr. Hawes is not within either of the
                    exceptions mentioned in the act of June 22, 1800; nor is it a case arising under
                    the twenty-fourth section of said act.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JNO. A. BINGHAM.</signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d421-a1.xml" xpointer="d421-a1"/>
